Runner: `{{runner}}` · Engine: `{{engine}}` · Revisions path: `{{migrations_path}}`

## 1. 3-Tier Environment Authority Model (`M2`)

| Environment Tier | Target Selector | Who May Execute Migration? | Mandatory Rule |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Tier 1 — Local / Disposable DB** | `{{local_selector}}` | **Agent (`code_writer` / `test_runner`)** | Agent runs autonomously to execute the full disposable-DB verification suite (`V1`–`V8` → `PASS` / `FAIL`). |
| **Tier 2 — Develop (`develop`)** | `{{develop_selector}}` | **Agent (ONLY on explicit User request)** _or_ **DevOps** | Agent **may** migrate `develop` **only when the user explicitly requests/approves it in the current session** (never autonomously). Agent **must** still generate the full Handoff Packet (`migration-handoff.md`). |
| **Tier 3 — Staging & Production (`staging`, `production`)** | `{{shared_selectors}}` | **Strictly DevOps** (**NEVER the Agent**) | Agent **never** executes schema or data migrations on `staging` or `production`, even if credentials exist. Agent prepares `migration-handoff.md` for the user to hand over to DevOps. |

## 2. Never-List (`M1`–`M5`, `M14`)

- **Never** run migrations on `staging` or `production` from the agent, or on `develop` without an explicit user command.
- **Never** deliver schema changes via `{{forbidden_commands}}` (reset, sync, `create_all`, manual DDL in SQL clients/MCP, or `stamp` to skip broken revisions).
- **Never** edit or delete a revision already applied to `develop`, `staging`, or `production` — always create a new forward revision.
- **Never** ship an autogenerated revision without reviewing every line, fixing renames, and adding `lock_timeout` / online index guards.
- **Never** embed connection strings, passwords, or customer PII in revisions, logs, or handoff packets.

## 3. Mandatory Rules (`M1`–`M14`)

| ID | Rule | Reference |
|---|---|---|
| **M1** | **Use the workspace's real runner & verify target host identity** before running any command. | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **M2** | **Enforce the 3-Tier Environment Authority Model** (`Local/Disposable` vs `Develop on user request` vs `Staging/Production by DevOps`). | [01]({{ref_01}}), [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **M3** | **Never use reset, sync, seed, or `create_all` as a migration path**. | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **M4** | **Roll out breaking changes via `Expand → Backfill → Contract`** across phases. | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **M5** | **Immutable, self-contained, single-head revisions** (no live app model imports inside revisions). | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **M6** | **Respect existing rows** (`server_default` or `NOT VALID` + `VALIDATE CONSTRAINT`). | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **M7** | **Guard locks & volume** (`SET LOCAL lock_timeout`, `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` outside transactions). | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **M8** | **Batched, resumable, tenant/scope-filtered, parameterized data backfills** (`B1`–`B8`). | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **M9** | **Verify `V1`–`V8` on a disposable database (`PASS` / `FAIL`)** with seeded multi-tenant data. | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **M10** | **Document pre-migration backup & explicit recovery steps** (rolling back code never rolls back data). | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **M11** | **Record canonical migration states** (`NOT_REQUIRED` \| `PENDING` \| `READY_FOR_HANDOFF` \| `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED` \| `VERIFIED_IN_TARGET` \| `FAILED`). | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **M12** | **Generate `migration-handoff.md` for every migration** (Summary of Changes & Why + step-by-step Schema & Data Runbook for `develop`, `staging`, and `production`). | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **M13** | **Separate infrastructure schema migrations from seed/business content**. | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **M14** | **Zero secrets or raw PII in revisions, commands, or handoff packets**. | [02]({{ref_02}}), [03]({{ref_03}}) |

## 4. Disposable-DB CLI Verification Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

| Gate | Command (`cwd: {{target_dir}}`) | Pass Criteria (`PASS` / `FAIL`) |
|---|---|---|
| **Clean Upgrade & Single Head** | `{{clean_install_and_heads_cmd}}` | `PASS` when exit `0` and exactly 1 head exists |
| **Zero Drift Check** | `{{drift_check_cmd}}` | `PASS` when models and revisions have zero un-migrated diffs |
| **Reversibility (`downgrade` / `upgrade`)** | `{{reversibility_cmd}}` | `PASS` when both `downgrade -1` and `upgrade head` exit `0` |
| **Automated Migration & Affected Tests** | `{{migration_test_cmd}}` | `PASS` when all migration and affected behavior tests pass |

